// A positional brace initializer on a GLOBAL struct used to silently zero the
// global (right fell through to the default-value Constant with the brace
// values discarded, no diagnostic, exit 0). The identical LOCAL spelling was
// already rejected by err_struct_positional_init.cb; this pins the global
// declarator now routing through the same diagnostic instead of disagreeing
// with the local scope.
expect_error("positional initializers are not supported for struct type 'GpiPoint'") {
    struct GpiPoint { int x; int y; };
    GpiPoint gpiPoint = {1, 2};
}

// The identical construct spelled without '=' ('GpiPoint2 p {1,2};') carries its
// brace list on a different grammar node (initDecl's own LeftBrace/initializerList,
// not initializer->initializerList()) - a guard keyed only on the '=' spelling
// would miss this one and the bug would survive under a one-character-different
// spelling. Same diagnostic, same reason.
expect_error("positional initializers are not supported for struct type 'GpiPoint2'") {
    struct GpiPoint2 { int x; int y; };
    GpiPoint2 gpiPoint2 {1, 2};
}
